The task: add authorization to `DocumentService.archive` in src/service.ts.

Rules:
- Actor has tenant, user, role: admin | editor | viewer.
- Only active documents in the actor's tenant are visible. Active = not deleted.
- Missing, deleted, foreign-tenant → Error('not found'), even for admin.
- Admin may archive any visible document; editor only one they own (document.owner === actor.user); viewer never.
- Unauthorized visible requests throw Error('forbidden').
- On success: set archived true and append exactly {actor: actor.user, document: id} to audit.
- Repeating archive on already archived visible document is no-op, but still enforce permission first (so an unauthorized archive on archived doc still throws).
